WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.292
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.592 --> 00:00:08.839
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:15.402
Unit twenty-one: Verb + Object + Infinitive. Today you will say what you want or expect others to do.

4
00:00:15.702 --> 00:00:18.331
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:22.407
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.019
Want.

7
00:00:25.017 --> 00:00:26.529
Want means to desire.

8
00:00:27.117 --> 00:00:28.385
I want you to come.

9
00:00:28.983 --> 00:00:31.241
Your turn. Say: Want.

10
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:34.997
Want.

11
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:36.612
Ask.

12
00:00:37.617 --> 00:00:39.314
Ask means to request.

13
00:00:39.917 --> 00:00:41.336
She asked me to help.

14
00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.788
Your turn. Say: Ask.

15
00:00:47.633 --> 00:00:48.553
Ask.

16
00:00:49.317 --> 00:00:50.132
Tell.

17
00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.698
Tell means to instruct.

18
00:00:53.283 --> 00:00:54.563
He told me to wait.

19
00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:57.675
Your turn. Say: Tell.

20
00:01:00.533 --> 00:01:01.116
Tell.

21
00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:02.921
Advise.

22
00:01:03.917 --> 00:01:05.823
Advise means to recommend.

23
00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:08.021
She advised me to rest.

24
00:01:08.617 --> 00:01:11.095
Your turn. Say: Advise.

25
00:01:13.933 --> 00:01:14.992
Advise.

26
00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:16.751
Expect.

27
00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:20.168
Expect means to think something will happen.

28
00:01:20.783 --> 00:01:22.504
I expect you to arrive.

29
00:01:23.117 --> 00:01:25.525
Your turn. Say: Expect.

30
00:01:28.367 --> 00:01:29.310
Expect.

31
00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:31.005
Allow.

32
00:01:32.017 --> 00:01:33.889
Allow means to give permission.

33
00:01:34.483 --> 00:01:35.984
They allow us to leave.

34
00:01:36.583 --> 00:01:38.794
Your turn. Say: Allow.

35
00:01:41.633 --> 00:01:42.646
Allow.

36
00:01:43.383 --> 00:01:44.268
Object.

37
00:01:45.283 --> 00:01:47.945
Object means the person who receives the action.

38
00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:49.807
Me is the object.

39
00:01:50.417 --> 00:01:52.965
Your turn. Say: Object.

40
00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:56.639
Object.

41
00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.593
Infinitive.

42
00:01:59.583 --> 00:02:01.896
Infinitive means to + base verb.

43
00:02:02.483 --> 00:02:03.450
To study.

44
00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:06.609
Your turn. Say: Infinitive.

45
00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:10.630
Infinitive.

46
00:02:11.433 --> 00:02:15.119
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:15.983 --> 00:02:18.308
Visal, what do your parents want you to do?

48
00:02:19.417 --> 00:02:30.361
My parents want me to study hard. The pattern is verb + object + to + base verb. The object is a person, and the infinitive tells what they should do.

49
00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:33.148
Which verbs use this pattern?

50
00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:47.482
Want, ask, tell, advise, expect, allow, and also invite, remind, warn and teach. She advised me to rest. The teacher allowed us to leave early.

51
00:02:48.583 --> 00:02:50.316
Is there a common mistake?

52
00:02:51.417 --> 00:03:00.738
Yes. We do not say I want that you come. We say I want you to come. And with make and let we use the base verb without to: She made me laugh.

53
00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:03.714
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:08.245
Grammar focus: Verb plus object plus to-infinitive.

55
00:03:08.545 --> 00:03:09.778
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:10.483 --> 00:03:12.576
My parents want me to study hard.

57
00:03:13.483 --> 00:03:15.135
She advised me to rest.

58
00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.108
The teacher allowed us to leave early.

59
00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:25.933
Verb + object + to + base verb. Never 'want that you…'. After make and let, use the base verb without to.

60
00:03:26.683 --> 00:03:30.021
Be careful! Don't say: I want that you come.

61
00:03:31.967 --> 00:03:33.606
Say: I want you to come.

62
00:03:33.906 --> 00:03:35.825
Use object + infinitive.

63
00:03:36.633 --> 00:03:39.576
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:41.937
Wanting Others to Act.

65
00:03:42.237 --> 00:03:44.294
My parents want me to study hard.

66
00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.369
My teacher asked me to read aloud.

67
00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:50.552
The doctor advised my father to rest.

68
00:03:51.567 --> 00:03:54.332
Our school allows students to use the library.

69
00:03:55.333 --> 00:03:57.333
I expect you to arrive on time.

70
00:03:58.433 --> 00:04:02.412
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:04.866
She wants blank to help her.

72
00:04:05.166 --> 00:04:08.216
A, I. B, me. C, my.

73
00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:13.534
The answer is B: me.

74
00:04:14.683 --> 00:04:16.358
He told us blank quietly.

75
00:04:16.658 --> 00:04:20.172
A, to speak. B, speak. C, speaking.

76
00:04:23.733 --> 00:04:25.663
The answer is A: to speak.

77
00:04:26.817 --> 00:04:28.004
Which is correct?

78
00:04:28.304 --> 00:04:33.188
A, I want that you stay.. B, I want you to stay.. C, I want you stay..

79
00:04:36.733 --> 00:04:39.081
The answer is B: I want you to stay..

80
00:04:40.217 --> 00:04:43.252
The teacher blank us to leave early. (gave permission)

81
00:04:43.552 --> 00:04:47.403
A, allowed. B, expected. C, warned.

82
00:04:50.967 --> 00:04:52.850
The answer is A: allowed.

83
00:04:54.017 --> 00:04:57.189
According to the reading, who advised the father to rest?

84
00:04:57.489 --> 00:05:01.293
A, the doctor. B, the teacher. C, the neighbour.

85
00:05:04.833 --> 00:05:06.705
The answer is A: the doctor.

86
00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:11.307
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:13.999
What do your parents want you to do?

88
00:05:22.783 --> 00:05:24.353
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:24.653 --> 00:05:36.875
My parents want me to study hard, and they expect me to help at home. My mother often asks me to cook, and my father advises me to save money. I use verb + object + to-infinitive.

90
00:05:37.175 --> 00:05:39.267
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:40.183 --> 00:05:45.076
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and verb plus object plus to-infinitive.

92
00:05:45.376 --> 00:05:49.445
Today's value is responsibility. Help at home and do your jobs.

93
00:05:49.745 --> 00:05:52.479
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

94
00:05:52.779 --> 00:05:55.582
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

